1
00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:07,570
When I was little, I wanted
to be a champion of justice.

2
00:00:08,370 --> 00:00:09,699
What?

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:10,949
You wanted to be one?

4
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:12,120
Did you give up?

5
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,410
Yeah.

6
00:00:13,411 --> 00:00:14,790
It's unfortunate, but...

7
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,709
Being a hero is a
limited-time thing.

8
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:21,299
When you grow up, it gets
hard to call yourself one.

9
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,760
I should have
realized that earlier.

10
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,299
I see.

11
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,930
That's just too bad, then.

12
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:30,889
Indeed.

13
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:32,350
You're absolutely right.

14
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:33,980
Yeah.

15
00:00:33,981 --> 00:00:37,190
Since you couldn't
do it, I'll do it for you.

16
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:40,819
You're an adult now,
so you can't do it.

17
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:42,570
But I can.

18
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:45,740
Just leave your dream to me.

19
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:49,450
Right.

20
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:52,290
Yeah.

21
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:54,540
I can be at peace now.

22
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:20,220
In the face of absolute despair

23
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:24,220
That nearly burned
our hearts away

24
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:30,770
You still found the
courage to smile

25
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:35,570
Like you accepted it all

26
00:01:36,370 --> 00:01:38,830
I lost my voice

27
00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:41,450
And the things I wanted to say

28
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:46,700
But every time I
fell to my knees

29
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:51,000
I stood up and kept walking

30
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:56,670
We were looking for
the ideal white future

31
00:01:56,880 --> 00:02:01,900
Our one and only hope

32
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:04,390
Now I may be left with nothing

33
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:09,810
But these raging
emotions that have

34
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:12,910
Nowhere to go

35
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:18,160
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

36
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:21,570
With more than one right answer

37
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:25,400
I won't stop

38
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,430
Until I find it

39
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:37,060
So what was this urgent
errand from Kuzuki-sensei?

40
00:02:37,061 --> 00:02:39,020
Dancing After School

41
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:38,350
I don't know.

42
00:02:38,890 --> 00:02:40,099
All she said was,

43
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:44,019
"I have to finish an errand from
Kuzuki-sensei tonight, or else.

44
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:48,649
Oh, and try to get along,
Sakura-chan and Saber-chan."

45
00:02:48,650 --> 00:02:52,529
She didn't go into detail.
She just left after that.

46
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:57,449
Jeez, she's the one who suggested
you stay over, and then she bails.

47
00:02:57,450 --> 00:03:02,330
But it's okay. It gave me a chance
to chat with Saber-san about things.

48
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:07,630
Yes. Sakura and I
have broken the ice.

49
00:03:13,470 --> 00:03:15,509
Come on, I'll be fine.

50
00:03:15,510 --> 00:03:18,349
There'll be lots of
people at school.

51
00:03:18,350 --> 00:03:22,480
Besides, didn't the school pass
your safety inspection yesterday?

52
00:03:22,890 --> 00:03:25,609
Shirou, that was yesterday.

53
00:03:25,610 --> 00:03:27,399
That doesn't mean
that it's still safe today.

54
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:30,899
If you're gonna be like that, I
won't ever be able to go anywhere.

55
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:35,780
And besides, you need to conserve
your mana, so get some rest.

56
00:03:39,950 --> 00:03:43,000
Very well, if that is
your decision, Master.

57
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:48,090
However, do not hesitate to use a Command
Spell if you think you're in danger.

58
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:50,170
Got it. See you later.

59
00:03:58,970 --> 00:03:59,970
Hey.

60
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:05,560
What? Do I have
something on my face?

61
00:04:13,110 --> 00:04:14,860
Self-Study

62
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,750
STUDENT COUNCIL ROOM

63
00:04:27,751 --> 00:04:30,250
Issei, aren't you
going to eat lunch?

64
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,169
I'll eat later.

65
00:04:33,170 --> 00:04:35,469
I just want to sleep right now.

66
00:04:35,470 --> 00:04:37,719
Oh? Did you stay up all night?

67
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:41,520
No, I just haven't been
sleeping well lately.

68
00:04:43,770 --> 00:04:45,599
Issei, someone's here.

69
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:49,480
I don't care! Tell them the
student council is closed!

70
00:04:51,230 --> 00:04:52,780
It's Kuzuki-sensei.

71
00:04:58,410 --> 00:05:00,370
Ryuudou, I need to speak to you.

72
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,700
Yes, sir.

73
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:08,460
Then she hasn't
returned home, either?

74
00:05:11,210 --> 00:05:12,999
I know.

75
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,509
Pardon the intrusion.

76
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:18,219
After-school activities are likely
to be canceled, so take note.

77
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:19,220
Yes, sir.

78
00:05:22,010 --> 00:05:23,719
What was that about?

79
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:24,720
Well...

80
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,270
Hey, Issei?

81
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:39,910
Well, you're not exactly an outsider,
so I guess it's okay for you to hear this.

82
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,529
Late last night,

83
00:05:42,530 --> 00:05:45,248
the faculty office got a
call from a family saying

84
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:48,209
their daughter hadn't come
home from archery practice.

85
00:05:48,210 --> 00:05:50,749
After calling the
other team members,

86
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:55,379
the teachers determined that Shinji was the
last one to talk to the missing student.

87
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:56,719
Shinji?

88
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:59,180
But Shinji wasn't at
practice yesterday.

89
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:02,600
Apparently, a first-year student
forgot something at the dojo,

90
00:06:03,050 --> 00:06:07,640
and when he came back for it, he saw
Shinji and the missing student arguing.

91
00:06:08,230 --> 00:06:10,849
We tried to confirm
this with Shinji.

92
00:06:10,850 --> 00:06:13,770
But he's absent today, and no
one's been able to reach him.

93
00:06:14,190 --> 00:06:17,070
Don't keep me in
suspense, Issei.

94
00:06:17,610 --> 00:06:19,820
Who's the missing student?

95
00:06:23,530 --> 00:06:24,870
Mitsuzuri Ayako,

96
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:27,450
the captain of the archery team.

97
00:06:30,750 --> 00:06:35,090
Did you notice anything odd
about Shinji's behavior yesterday?

98
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:38,049
I'm sorry, Senpai.

99
00:06:38,050 --> 00:06:40,840
I haven't seen him
very often lately either.

100
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:45,059
That's right. You
wouldn't know anything.

101
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:47,599
Sorry, I shouldn't
have asked you that.

102
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:50,269
No, that's not true.

103
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:53,939
I know my brother
better than anyone.

104
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:56,780
Well, it's not something
you should be worrying about.

105
00:06:57,570 --> 00:06:58,570
See you.

106
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:14,669
All after-school club
activities are canceled today.

107
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:17,049
The library will also be closed.

108
00:07:17,050 --> 00:07:21,549
Students with no urgent business are
asked to leave school grounds at once.

109
00:07:21,550 --> 00:07:22,800
I repeat...

110
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:27,059
If you're looking for Ayako-chan,
she's home sick today.

111
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:29,519
Oh, thanks.

112
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:33,019
If Mitsuzuri comes tomorrow,
don't mention this, okay?

113
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:34,150
Okay...

114
00:08:00,670 --> 00:08:02,130
Huh? Tohsaka?

115
00:08:02,510 --> 00:08:04,179
Unbelievable.

116
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:07,259
Are you crazy, coming to
school without your Servant?

117
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,889
What choice did I have?

118
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:11,679
Saber can't dematerialize,
so I can't bring her.

119
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:14,389
Then stay home from school.

120
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:17,769
A Master strolling
around without his Servant

121
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:20,609
might as well have "Please
kill me" painted on his back.

122
00:08:20,610 --> 00:08:24,070
Emiya-kun, do you have any
idea just how big of an idiot you are?

123
00:08:24,650 --> 00:08:26,159
Idiot?

124
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:29,119
Masters don't fight with
other people around, right?

125
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:31,450
So it should be
perfectly safe at school.

126
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:34,210
Then tell me this:

127
00:08:34,830 --> 00:08:37,079
do you see anyone else here?

128
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,250
Huh?

129
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,090
Wait...

130
00:08:43,670 --> 00:08:46,049
Finally sinking in, I see.

131
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:49,800
Seriously, this morning, I went
from exasperated to furious.

132
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:54,640
"After all I told him, why is he doing
everything he can to get himself killed?"

133
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:56,269
A magic crest...

134
00:08:56,270 --> 00:09:00,859
Yes, this is the manifestation of
the magic passed down in my family.

135
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:06,400
I can invoke any spell etched here
by simply passing mana through it.

136
00:09:07,030 --> 00:09:08,819
I've sent Archer away.

137
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:12,369
The Gandr Shot here
will suffice for you.

138
00:09:12,370 --> 00:09:15,290
Gandr? Isn't that just
a simple Nordic curse?

139
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:19,669
That's right. A
perfectly simple curse.

140
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:21,129
W-Wait, Tohsaka!

141
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:24,209
Are you crazy? We're at school!

142
00:09:24,210 --> 00:09:26,759
If we make a scene, who
knows who might turn up?

143
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,799
I'll worry about that
when it happens.

144
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:32,140
My policy is not to miss an
opportunity when it presents itself.

145
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:36,640
Sorry, Emiya-kun, but I'll
take you out here and now.

146
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:42,149
Besides, I don't think my nerves could
take much more of your bumbling around.

147
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:44,109
Wait, damn it!

148
00:09:44,110 --> 00:09:46,439
I don't want to fight you...

149
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:48,489
Well, I want to fight you!

150
00:09:48,490 --> 00:09:51,370
Just prepare yourself, Shirou!

151
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:57,960
That was Gandr?

152
00:09:58,330 --> 00:10:01,129
It's nothing like the one I
know! Are you trying to kill me?

153
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:03,549
I thought I made that clear!

154
00:10:03,550 --> 00:10:05,670
Hold it right there!

155
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:08,840
Ow!

156
00:10:10,430 --> 00:10:13,099
You could seriously hurt
someone with those things!

157
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:15,519
If you're scared of a
little pain, just stand still!

158
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,809
I'll finish you off quickly!

159
00:10:17,810 --> 00:10:19,770
If they hit a vital spot,
you'll die instantly!

160
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:28,029
That doesn't sound
like a mercy killing!

161
00:10:28,030 --> 00:10:30,450
Shut up! Then
quit running around!

162
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:34,370
I'm getting worked up because
my target won't stand still!

163
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,040
Oh, crap!

164
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:55,560
- Das Schließen Vogelkäfig... Echo!
- The locking, bird cage... Echo!

165
00:11:02,810 --> 00:11:04,860
She put up a magic field!

166
00:11:08,190 --> 00:11:09,400
Fixierung, Eilsalve!

167
00:11:09,401 --> 00:11:10,609
Fixation, speed volley!

168
00:11:10,610 --> 00:11:12,280
Trace on!

169
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:32,510
She's out of mana?

170
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:05,380
So you finally came
out, Emiya-kun?

171
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:11,799
Put down that silly weapon.

172
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,010
You don't have a chance
of winning, Emiya-kun.

173
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:17,510
I won't know until I try.

174
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:20,099
Oh, really?

175
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:22,019
Well, this is your
final warning.

176
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:25,269
Put down your weapon, and
hold out your Command Spells.

177
00:12:25,270 --> 00:12:27,584
At worst, I'll strip
the nerves from your

178
00:12:27,596 --> 00:12:30,149
arm, but better to lose
those than your life.

179
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:32,440
No. I will not give you
the Command Spells.

180
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:36,320
That's no different from
telling me to betray Saber.

181
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:37,820
I see.

182
00:12:38,370 --> 00:12:39,869
I'll give you three seconds.

183
00:12:39,870 --> 00:12:42,830
It's your life, so
it's your decision.

184
00:12:48,210 --> 00:12:51,840
Time's up. Emiya-kun,
what's your decision?

185
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,929
Tohsaka, was that...

186
00:12:55,930 --> 00:12:57,679
A scream?

187
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,970
Wait, Emiya-kun!

188
00:13:03,470 --> 00:13:05,390
It looks like she's
just unconscious.

189
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:11,480
She isn't just unconscious! Can't
you see she's been drained dry?

190
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:13,819
Drained dry?

191
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:17,239
Of her mana. Her
life force, if you like.

192
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,990
She hardly has any blood left.

193
00:13:19,530 --> 00:13:21,870
If we don't do
something, she'll die.

194
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:24,619
Die? Hey, Tohsaka...

195
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:27,210
I should be able to
stabilize her with this gem.

196
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,889
Tohsaka...

197
00:13:39,890 --> 00:13:40,890
Look out!

198
00:13:44,930 --> 00:13:47,520
Wh-What is that?

199
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:53,979
Why did you...

200
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:58,279
Never mind that, you're
bleeding! You're bleeding badly!

201
00:13:58,280 --> 00:14:00,279
D-Doesn't it hurt?

202
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:02,660
It does. Like you
wouldn't believe.

203
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:07,499
Tohsaka, take care of her.

204
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,500
Wha...

205
00:14:29,190 --> 00:14:30,190
A Servant!

206
00:14:31,850 --> 00:14:33,150
She vanished?

207
00:14:38,950 --> 00:14:42,949
I'm surprised. You aren't
going to use a Command Spell?

208
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:46,040
Sorry. I don't have many left.

209
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:47,829
I see.

210
00:14:47,830 --> 00:14:51,249
Unlike my Master,
you possess courage.

211
00:14:51,250 --> 00:14:54,539
In that case, I will take
a different approach.

212
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:58,300
I shall grant you
a merciful death.

213
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:12,769
Compared to the other Servants,
you aren't very impressive.

214
00:15:12,770 --> 00:15:14,270
You don't pack any punch.

215
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:17,399
No, this is the end for you.

216
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:21,650
I've had you in the palm
of my hand all along.

217
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:32,330
Now, then. What was that interesting
thing you were saying before?

218
00:15:33,210 --> 00:15:37,460
Something about my being
inferior to other Servants?

219
00:15:38,090 --> 00:15:39,960
I'm afraid we can't have that.

220
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:47,400
I'll start by plucking out those
eyes that were so dearly mistaken.

221
00:15:47,890 --> 00:15:50,270
Then I'll move on to your limbs.

222
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:01,490
Emiya-kun, are you all right?

223
00:16:03,570 --> 00:16:05,870
W-We have to stop the bleeding!

224
00:16:07,030 --> 00:16:09,789
Emiya-kun, do you have
anything I can wrap it with?

225
00:16:09,790 --> 00:16:13,329
Uh... Oh, I have a handkerchief.

226
00:16:13,330 --> 00:16:15,420
Sakura always
prepares one for me.

227
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:18,249
Like minds, huh?

228
00:16:18,250 --> 00:16:19,999
But it's better than nothing.

229
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,800
Together with my
towel, we can make do.

230
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:28,600
So, that woman was a Servant?

231
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:31,470
Yeah. She attacked
out of nowhere.

232
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,519
Don't look at me like that.

233
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,928
I couldn't tell who it
was, but doesn't that

234
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:40,360
mean there's another
Master here besides us?

235
00:16:41,070 --> 00:16:43,650
They've finally made
their move, huh?

236
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:47,569
Okay, I've patched
you up for now.

237
00:16:47,570 --> 00:16:50,119
Tohsaka, what
happened with that girl?

238
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:53,369
She's recovering. I
think she'll pull through.

239
00:16:53,370 --> 00:16:54,370
Ah.

240
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,290
That's good.

241
00:17:01,210 --> 00:17:04,299
Why are you staring
at me like that?

242
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:07,549
J-Just so you know, I'd
never do something like that!

243
00:17:07,550 --> 00:17:10,509
Listen, I know.

244
00:17:10,510 --> 00:17:12,600
You'd never do that.

245
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:16,139
I'm talking about our fight.

246
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:17,140
Want to continue?

247
00:17:21,690 --> 00:17:23,900
Tohsaka? I mean...

248
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:26,399
What do you want to do?

249
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:29,619
No, thanks. Let's call it a day.

250
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:31,490
For one thing, I owe you again.

251
00:17:32,030 --> 00:17:33,659
Okay, let's go.

252
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:35,999
We need to get
your wound treated.

253
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,120
Please bear with it
until we get to my place.

254
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:42,000
Your place?

255
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:49,889
Put simply, there's
another Master at school

256
00:17:49,890 --> 00:17:54,219
who's preyed on many
students like that girl.

257
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,890
Why would they do that?

258
00:17:56,230 --> 00:17:58,939
To win the Holy
Grail War, of course.

259
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:03,439
Their plan is to sacrifice the students
to strengthen their own Servant.

260
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:04,780
Are they nuts?

261
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:09,859
Who knows? But there's already a
magical field set up around the school.

262
00:18:09,860 --> 00:18:15,040
Once it's activated, it will probably
drain the life force from everyone inside.

263
00:18:16,450 --> 00:18:17,540
Emiya-kun...

264
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,120
Coming from me,
you might reject this,

265
00:18:21,170 --> 00:18:23,130
but I think we
should call a truce.

266
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:27,379
A truce? Between you and me?

267
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:31,139
I want to deal with
this other Master first.

268
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:35,220
So until then, want to call a truce
and help me track them down?

269
00:18:35,850 --> 00:18:38,849
Well? Personally, I
think it's a good deal.

270
00:18:38,850 --> 00:18:42,400
Sure, having your help will
make me feel a lot better.

271
00:18:42,770 --> 00:18:48,739
I'm not really helping you. We've
simply agreed to a ceasefire.

272
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:54,029
But as long as you don't betray
me, I'll assist you, Emiya-kun.

273
00:18:54,030 --> 00:18:59,210
So we'll be partners for life,
then. Let's do our best, Tohsaka.

274
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:06,500
It won't be quite that long,
but try to make yourself useful.

275
00:19:09,670 --> 00:19:10,680
Now I understand.

276
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:14,719
You aren't a legitimate heir.

277
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:18,310
Your father died before he could
pass his magic crest on to you.

278
00:19:18,970 --> 00:19:20,729
I'm not so sure.

279
00:19:20,730 --> 00:19:24,440
He was always against
my becoming a mage.

280
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:27,479
Isn't that contradictory?

281
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,979
Maybe.

282
00:19:28,980 --> 00:19:33,570
It always seemed like Dad only
taught me because I refused to give up.

283
00:19:34,410 --> 00:19:38,119
In the end, he only
taught me fortifying magic,

284
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,580
so that's all I can use.

285
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:43,460
Hold on! Why would
you tell me that?

286
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:46,000
Tohsaka?

287
00:19:47,090 --> 00:19:50,509
Look, Emiya-kun, we might
be partners for the time being,

288
00:19:50,510 --> 00:19:54,339
but mages should always
keep their arts a secret.

289
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:57,219
What's the point
of hiding it now?

290
00:19:57,220 --> 00:20:01,230
Dad always said that magic isn't something
you should go out of your way to hide.

291
00:20:04,230 --> 00:20:05,860
He really said that?

292
00:20:06,230 --> 00:20:10,440
Yeah. I think he was trying to tell
me not to let myself be bound by rules.

293
00:20:10,990 --> 00:20:14,359
He always said I should
quit if I ever want to.

294
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:18,159
That's ridiculous! Your
father was no mage!

295
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:21,619
And if he trained you, you're
no mage either in my eyes!

296
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:23,659
Why are you so upset?

297
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:28,630
I know I can't call myself a mage,
but my dad was the real deal.

298
00:20:29,130 --> 00:20:31,959
That's not what I mean.

299
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,510
I'm trying to say...

300
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:36,390
Well...

301
00:20:38,890 --> 00:20:42,770
Yeah, I do have a problem
with your incompetence.

302
00:20:43,390 --> 00:20:46,809
What can I do?
My old man's dead.

303
00:20:46,810 --> 00:20:50,649
Yeah, that's the inherent
limit of a single mage.

304
00:20:50,650 --> 00:20:55,650
Mages never know when they'll die,
so they leave behind a magic crest.

305
00:20:56,280 --> 00:21:02,540
I was just angry at your father for
not taking the proper steps to prepare.

306
00:21:04,290 --> 00:21:07,369
Magic is the culmination
of lifetimes of work,

307
00:21:07,370 --> 00:21:10,710
handed down from parent to
child for generation after generation.

308
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,589
The instant a child is
born into a mage family,

309
00:21:14,590 --> 00:21:18,510
that child inherits not only
their legacy but also their duty.

310
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:23,270
That's the reason we're
born, and it's what we die for.

311
00:21:26,190 --> 00:21:31,069
A mage family's duty is to take
the human child they gave birth to

312
00:21:31,070 --> 00:21:35,070
and turn it into something else
over long years of rigorous training.

313
00:21:35,820 --> 00:21:39,410
That's why your father
was no mage, Emiya-kun.

314
00:21:40,030 --> 00:21:45,960
He put being a father
ahead of being a mage.

315
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:16,509
We didn't understand anything

316
00:22:16,510 --> 00:22:22,679
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

317
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:25,679
A moral conflict

318
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:28,480
stays your hand

319
00:22:28,730 --> 00:22:31,229
and tricks you

320
00:22:31,230 --> 00:22:33,110
out of your future

321
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:40,029
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

322
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:45,830
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

323
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:54,040
but I want to live my life

324
00:22:55,040 --> 00:23:00,049
The past repeats before my eyes

325
00:23:00,050 --> 00:23:07,849
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

326
00:23:07,850 --> 00:23:13,939
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

327
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:19,569
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

328
00:23:19,570 --> 00:23:23,280
Fight your fate

329
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:29,179
Is this Ryuudou Temple?

330
00:23:29,180 --> 00:23:31,439
Please don't be so stiff, Emiya.

331
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:34,099
All the people in this
town belong to me.

332
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:37,229
I may be inexperienced,
but I am still a mage.

333
00:23:37,230 --> 00:23:40,570
If you wish to pass, then
force your way through.

334
00:23:37,230 --> 00:23:39,110
Mirage

335
00:23:39,111 --> 00:23:40,990
Next Time

